<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy — LanDeng" description="How LanDeng (Zhangjiakou Landeng Technology Co., Ltd.) handles personal information on incenseherbs.com — what we collect, cookies, third parties, retention, cross-border transfer, and your GDPR/CCPA rights.">
  <article class="article">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p><em>Last updated: 2026-10-21 · Applies to incenseherbs.com and data.incenseherbs.com</em></p>

    <blockquote>
      This is a static knowledge platform. We do not run analytics, advertising, or behavioural
      tracking on these pages, and we collect personal information only when you choose to contact us.
      This policy says exactly what we collect, what we do not, and who else may process data in the
      course of serving the site.
    </blockquote>

    <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      LanDeng (澜灯) is a brand operated by <strong>Zhangjiakou Landeng Technology Co., Ltd.</strong>
      (USCC 91130702MAKM4QXH5Q), Room 202, Unit 4, Building 14, Linli Jiayuan, No. 1 Gongye East
      Street, Qiaodong District, Zhangjiakou, Hebei, China. For the purposes of data-protection law,
      we are the controller of the limited personal information described in this policy.
      Our contact for privacy matters is <a href="mailto:landengltd@gmail.com">landengltd@gmail.com</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>2. What we collect — item by item</h2>
    <p>
      We collect personal information in three ways only, each of which you initiate. If a channel is
      not listed here, we do not use it.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Email inquiries.</strong> The site directs inquiries to
        <code>landengltd@gmail.com</code>. When you email us, we receive whatever you choose to send —
        typically your name, email address, company, country, product interest, quantity, and message.
        We use it solely to respond to your inquiry and to keep a record of business correspondence.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>WhatsApp, phone, and WeChat inquiries.</strong> The site links to WhatsApp
        (<code>wa.me/8613323237275</code>) and lists the number +86 13323237275, which also serves
        phone and WeChat. If you message or call, we receive your phone number and the content you
        send, and we use it only to respond to your inquiry. WhatsApp is operated by a third party,
        Meta; when you use that channel, Meta's own privacy terms apply to your use of their service,
        in addition to this policy.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Server and access logs.</strong> Like any website, our hosting provider records
        standard technical logs — IP address, browser type, pages requested, and timestamps — needed
        to serve pages, maintain security, and prevent abuse. We host on Cloudflare's network, so
        Cloudflare processes these logs on our behalf. These logs are not used to build profiles of
        visitors and are not combined with your inquiry data.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>3. What we do not collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>No accounts, no logins.</strong> This site has no user accounts and no
        registration.</li>
      <li><strong>No cookies, no trackers, no analytics.</strong> These are static pages. We set no
        cookies and load no third-party tracking, advertising, or analytics scripts.</li>
      <li><strong>No online forms or payment.</strong> The inquiry form is not yet live, and there is
        no online ordering or payment processing on this site. If that changes, we will update this
        policy first.</li>
      <li><strong>No marketing lists.</strong> We do not run newsletters or send marketing email.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>4. Cookies</h2>
    <p>
      We do not use cookies for tracking, analytics, advertising, or any other purpose. Because there
      are no cookies to manage, there is no cookie banner and no cookie settings. The only third-party
      resources your browser requests are the site's webfonts (see section 5), and those requests do
      not involve our setting any cookie on your device.
    </p>
    <p>
      Because we run no tracking and set no cookies, browser "Do Not Track" signals have no effect —
      there is nothing to turn off. You can read the site in full without providing any personal
      information or accepting any cookie.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Third parties that process data on our behalf</h2>
    <p>
      A small number of third parties are involved in serving the site or receiving your inquiries.
      They process data as described below; none of them sells your data, and we do not sell it either.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Cloudflare (hosting and CDN).</strong> The site is served through Cloudflare's network,
        which processes the technical access logs in section 2. Cloudflare's privacy policy applies to
        its handling of that technical data.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Google Fonts.</strong> The site loads its typefaces from Google's font servers
        (<code>fonts.googleapis.com</code> / <code>fonts.gstatic.com</code>). When your browser fetches
        these fonts, Google may receive your IP address and basic browser metadata, as described in
        Google's privacy policy.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Google (email).</strong> Our published contact address is hosted by Google. Email you
        send to us is handled by Google's mail service, so Google processes it as an email provider.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Meta (WhatsApp).</strong> If you contact us through WhatsApp, Meta processes your
        messages and phone number under Meta's terms and privacy policy.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We do not otherwise share, rent, or sell your personal information, and we do not pass your
      inquiry details to brokers or advertisers.
    </p>

    <h2>6. How we use information, and the legal basis</h2>
    <p>
      Inquiry information is used only to answer you and, if you proceed, to prepare quotes, samples,
      or order documentation. We do not use it for marketing without your request.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Where the GDPR applies, we process your inquiry on the basis of
        <strong>legitimate interest</strong> (responding to a message you sent us) and, where you
        proceed to a business discussion, steps toward a contract you requested.</li>
      <li>Using WhatsApp is your choice; by messaging us there you consent to the handling of your
        message through that third-party channel, and you can withdraw that consent by not using that
        channel or by asking us to delete the correspondence.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>7. Retention</h2>
    <p>
      We keep business correspondence only as long as needed to answer you and to meet record-keeping,
      warranty, or commercial obligations — and no longer. Technical access logs are retained by our
      hosting provider for a short period for security and operational purposes, and are not used to
      identify individual visitors. If you ask us to delete your correspondence, we will do so unless a
      legal or contractual obligation requires us to keep it (for example, completed order records we
      must retain for accounting or tax reasons). Where a deletion request is refused for one of those
      reasons, we will tell you why.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Cross-border transfer</h2>
    <p>
      We are based in China, and the site is read worldwide. The third parties in section 5 —
      Cloudflare, Google, and Meta — operate global networks, which means the data described above may
      be processed on servers in the United States, the European Economic Area, or elsewhere outside
      your country and outside China. Where a transfer is subject to data-protection law, we rely on
      the lawful mechanisms those providers offer, such as the EU standard contractual clauses
      incorporated into their terms. By emailing or messaging us, you acknowledge that your inquiry
      crosses these borders.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Depending on where you are located, privacy laws such as the EU/UK General Data Protection
      Regulation (GDPR) or the California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA/CPRA) give you certain rights over
      the personal information we hold. Because we collect only the inquiry data you choose to send us
      and keep no profiles, these rights are straightforward to honour:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Access</strong> — request a copy of the personal information we hold about you.</li>
      <li><strong>Correction</strong> — ask us to correct inaccurate or incomplete information.</li>
      <li><strong>Deletion</strong> — ask us to delete your information, unless a legal or contractual
        obligation requires us to retain it.</li>
      <li><strong>Portability</strong> — where applicable, receive your information in a structured,
        commonly used, machine-readable format.</li>
      <li><strong>Withdraw consent / object</strong> — stop using a consent-based channel such as
        WhatsApp, or object to processing based on legitimate interest.</li>
      <li><strong>No sale / no "sale or share" opt-out needed</strong> — we do not sell or share your
        personal information for cross-context behavioural advertising, and have not done so in the
        preceding 12 months, so there is no opt-out to exercise under CCPA/CPRA.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      To exercise any of these rights, write to
      <a href="mailto:landengltd@gmail.com">landengltd@gmail.com</a>. We aim to respond within 30 days
      (or the period the applicable law requires) and will verify your identity before releasing
      information. We do not sell your personal information and have not sold it in the preceding 12
      months, so there is no "do not sell" opt-out to exercise — but we will honour any of the rights
      above on request. We will not discriminate against you for exercising a right. If you are in the
      EEA or UK, you may also lodge a complaint with your local data-protection supervisory authority.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Children's privacy</h2>
    <p>
      The site is not directed at children, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from
      anyone under the age of 16. If you are a parent or guardian and believe a child has sent us
      personal information, contact us and we will delete it.
    </p>

    <h2>11. Security</h2>
    <p>
      We collect minimal personal information and hold none of it in an account system on this site.
      The site is served over HTTPS, so content is encrypted in transit, and the email channel is
      provided by Google with its own security controls. We do not collect payment details and
      therefore store no card or financial data. We restrict access to inquiry correspondence to the
      people who need it to respond. No method of transmission is completely secure; email is not
      encrypted end-to-end, so avoid sending sensitive information you would not want intercepted.
    </p>

    <h2>12. Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      If we ever add forms, analytics, or other data-processing features, we will update this policy
      first and change its date. The version you are reading describes the site as it operates today,
      and its "last updated" date is 2026-10-21.
    </p>

    <h2>13. Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about this policy, or any privacy request:
      <a href="mailto:landengltd@gmail.com">landengltd@gmail.com</a>. Related pages:
      <a href="/disclaimer/">Disclaimer</a> · <a href="/terms-of-service/">Terms of Service</a> ·
      <a href="/safety/">Safety</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
